#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Randomized incremental builds: Blaze on a kept graph against the oracle and a clean Blaze build.

usage: scripts/incremental/fuzz help
       scripts/incremental/fuzz kinds
       scripts/incremental/fuzz run [--blaze B] [--oracle O] [--rounds N] [--seed S]
                                    [--failsafe on|off] [--keep]

Three sides, each with its own copy of a generated workspace under
~/.cache/blaze/work/i3/fuzz/<seed>/<side>/ (ws, the local modules ext and ext2, a second package
path root pp, a repository override ovr) and its own output user root:

  A  Blaze, BLAZE_SERVER_MODE=daemon: the server keeps its graph (the side under test);
  O  the oracle (~/.cache/blaze/oracle/bazel-9.3.2-linux-x86_64), a server with its state kept;
  B  Blaze in process (no server) with BLAZE_INCREMENTAL=none and `clean` before every build.

Each round picks one edit (`kinds` lists them), applies the same edit to the three workspaces,
sometimes tampers with an output in A's and O's bazel-bin (a file, a tree artifact's file or a
runfiles entry), sometimes runs another command on A and O first (query, cquery, test, fetch),
then runs the round's build (`build --keep_going //...` with the options the edits have set) on
the three sides and compares:

  vs oracle (counted): the exit code; every file under bazel-bin, both ways (path, sha256, exec
    bit, symlink target with the output root and workspace normalised), except compiler
    intermediates (_objs, .d, .o, .a, .so, .params, .cppmap, manifests, .repo_mapping); the
    stdout of query and cquery and the exit code of the other commands.
  vs clean (counted unless A agrees with O there, i.e. Bazel keeps the same stale state): the
    exit code, the ERROR and WARNING lines as sets, and every file of B's bazel-bin (A must have
    it with the same sha256 and exec bit).
  The ERROR and WARNING lines against the oracle are printed (msgdiff) but not counted: the
    Starlark interpreter's error texts differ by the user's decision (starlark-rust).

Round-2 review additions: a fixed --invocation_id on stretches of rounds (all sides; while it
is on, differences against the oracle are printed and not counted: Bazel 9.3.2 gives stale
results or crashes on a repeated id); --watchfs on
stretches of rounds with directory renames, re-creations and removals; writes racing the start of
A's command (the racing round is not compared; the next build of all sides is, with no edit in
between); SIGINT during A's build (the same). Interrupts and races apply to A only.

Servers: A and O only (two at once), startup --max_idle_secs=900 with a `.keep-server` file in
their output roots while the run lasts; builds use --jobs=4. Both are shut down at the end.
Heavy: run under `systemd-run --user --collect --wait -p MemoryMax=12G -p MemorySwapMax=0`.
--failsafe off sets BLAZE_INCREMENTAL_REMOTE_FAILSAFE=off for A (debug builds only).
The log is ~/.cache/blaze/work/i3/fuzz/<seed>/log.txt; directories are deleted unless --keep.
"""

